&lt;p&gt;Secure Every AI Interaction.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Josh Colvin is the founder and sole developer of AegisGate Security, LLC. 8 provisional patents filed. Over 1.1M LOC across 5 products. Apache 2.0. No telemetry. No data egress. &lt;a href="https://github.com/aegisgatesecurity/aegisgate-platform" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Last week I wrote about &lt;a href="https://dev.to/selcukgural/i-built-kule-ai-agents-work-on-a-copy-of-your-folder-and-you-decide-what-comes-back-1ik2"&gt;Kule&lt;/a&gt;, the open-source tool I'm building. Your comments turned into real changes, so this time I'd like to ask for something more specific: &lt;strong&gt;try Kule on your own computer, and tell me what happened.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Kule in one paragraph
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Kule is a control room for AI agents that work on your folders. You point an agent (Claude Code, Codex, Gemini, or any agent that speaks &lt;a href="https://agentclientprotocol.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;ACP&lt;/a&gt;) at a folder. Kule gives it a copy-on-write copy of that folder inside an OS sandbox, looks at what every command really changed, and lets nothing reach the real folder until a policy, or you, says so. Every commit can be undone. It has a CLI and a desktop app, it's written in Rust, and it's Apache-2.0.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What changed since the first post
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That post covered &lt;code&gt;0.2.0-preview.1&lt;/code&gt;. The latest is &lt;code&gt;0.2.0-preview.14&lt;/code&gt;. Some of the bigger changes:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The default policy is an allow-list now.&lt;/strong&gt; Files of a kind known not to run by themselves, or of a kind your project already tracks, pass on their own. Everything else waits for you, scripts and hidden files included.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Nothing an agent writes reaches your home.&lt;/strong&gt; Agents keep their settings, history and transcripts in a home of their own inside Kule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;A task's commands can't read your other projects&lt;/strong&gt;, or where apps keep their settings, sign-ins and data, beyond what toolchains and shells need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Your terminals run in the task's sandbox too&lt;/strong&gt;, not just the agent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Kule tells you what it cut, ended or refused&lt;/strong&gt;, where you're working: in the command's output, the terminal, and the app's Live view.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Releases are built on pinned images&lt;/strong&gt; and can't be changed once they're published. Each one comes with checksums, a build provenance attestation and an SBOM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;15 security advisories are published so far.&lt;/strong&gt; Each one went out after its fix had shipped.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Some of these came straight from comments on the first post:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An approval card now says whether Kule looks inside the connection you're approving (&lt;a href="https://github.com/kulehq/kule/issues/27" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;#27&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;I measured which tools send Encrypted Client Hello before deciding how Kule treats it (&lt;a href="https://github.com/kulehq/kule/issues/34" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;#34&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Holding a &lt;code&gt;git push&lt;/code&gt; apart from fetches is next (&lt;a href="https://github.com/kulehq/kule/issues/50" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;#50&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thank you to everyone who asked those questions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What I'm asking for
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I wrote a short &lt;a href="https://kulehq.github.io/kule/docs/testing" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;testing guide&lt;/a&gt; with six scenarios. Each takes 5 to 20 minutes, and you can pick any of them:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Install and check.&lt;/strong&gt; Does the install guide hold up on your machine?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The loop, without an agent.&lt;/strong&gt; Make a task, change the copy, review, commit, undo. No network or agent needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The app, with an agent.&lt;/strong&gt; Your first task in the desktop app, from prompt to commit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Your own work.&lt;/strong&gt; Ask an agent for something you'd ask it anyway, and see whether Kule gets in the way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Your own setup.&lt;/strong&gt; This is where I need help most (more on that below).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The boundaries.&lt;/strong&gt; Try to get past them, and report what you find privately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At the end of each one, there's only one question: &lt;strong&gt;what happened that you didn't expect?&lt;/strong&gt; A confusing step, a policy that asks too often, a tool that breaks inside the sandbox, a slow copy: all of it is useful. "Everything worked" is useful too.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Setups I can't test myself
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Kule is tested on a handful of machines. If yours is one of these, a short report is worth a lot:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a Linux distribution other than Ubuntu, or Ubuntu 24.04 with its user namespace restriction;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a file system other than APFS, Btrfs or XFS;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a large repository or a monorepo;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;an Intel Mac;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;an ACP agent other than Claude Code, Codex and Gemini.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Before you start
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;macOS 13+ and Linux x86_64 only.&lt;/strong&gt; Windows support is in progress, but it's not ready for testing yet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The macOS app isn't notarized.&lt;/strong&gt; It's signed ad hoc, so macOS will refuse to open it the first time. The &lt;a href="https://kulehq.github.io/kule/docs/getting-started/install" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;install guide&lt;/a&gt; shows how to check the download and open the app.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Start with a test folder&lt;/strong&gt;, or with a project whose work is all committed and pushed. Kule doesn't touch your folder until you commit, but it's still a preview.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Agents use your own accounts&lt;/strong&gt;, so a run spends your own quota or API credit, the same as it would without Kule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  How to report
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Open an issue at &lt;a href="https://github.com/kulehq/kule/issues/new/choose" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;github.com/kulehq/kule/issues/new/choose&lt;/a&gt; and pick one of the forms: &lt;strong&gt;Bug report&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Test report&lt;/strong&gt; or &lt;strong&gt;Idea or change&lt;/strong&gt;. Questions are welcome in &lt;a href="https://github.com/kulehq/kule/discussions" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Discussions&lt;/a&gt;, or right here in the comments.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Issues are public, so please leave out API keys, tokens, private paths and anything else you wouldn't publish. The forms remind you.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you find a way past one of Kule's boundaries, please don't post it publicly.&lt;/strong&gt; Report it privately, as &lt;a href="https://github.com/kulehq/kule/blob/main/SECURITY.md" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;SECURITY.md&lt;/a&gt; explains. The fix is made in private and released first, and the advisory credits you unless you'd rather it didn't.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What happens next
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I read every report. A fix ships in the next preview, and its issue says which one. The &lt;a href="https://github.com/kulehq/kule/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;CHANGELOG&lt;/a&gt; lists what each preview changed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Testing guide:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://kulehq.github.io/kule/docs/testing" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;kulehq.github.io/kule/docs/testing&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Download:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://github.com/kulehq/kule/releases" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;releases page&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Code:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://github.com/kulehq/kule" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;github.com/kulehq/kule&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thanks for reading, and thanks in advance to anyone who gives it 15 minutes. 🙏&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Short answer: keep the original image in object storage under an application-owned, user-scoped key, and treat the database as the authority for retention and deletion. For a media service processing receipts, large-file throughput should decide the upload path first; lifecycle cleanup and user-requested deletion are separate controls with separate SLOs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The useful design is boring: one immutable object key per source file, a small record describing that object, bounded workers, and an audit trail for every deletion decision. A folder is only a prefix in a flat object namespace. It is not an access-control boundary, a transaction, or a substitute for metadata.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  How should I store generated images per user folder?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use a key that is difficult to confuse with another receipt, for example &lt;code&gt;users/{userID}/receipts/{receiptID}/original.png&lt;/code&gt;. Generate &lt;code&gt;receiptID&lt;/code&gt; server-side, store the complete key in the database, and keep the original separate from derived previews. A per-user prefix makes an operational listing possible, but deletion should use the recorded key rather than infer intent from a filename or prompt. I don't regard the prefix as authorization; the API still needs an authorization check against the user ID in the record.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The record should include the user identifier, object key, byte size, content type, upload state, creation time, retention deadline, and a deletion-request timestamp. Keep generation and receipt-processing state there too. Object storage is good at durable bytes; it is a poor place to discover why a file exists.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use a direct, explicit delete for a user request or a legal-retention transition. Use a lifecycle rule for material that is allowed to expire by age, such as failed intermediates or temporary derivatives. Do not promise an hour-level deletion SLO from a day-granularity lifecycle policy. If the policy requires removal sooner, the application worker owns that deadline and must report it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There is a sharp boundary here. Lifecycle is housekeeping. Deletion intent is a business event.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That distinction is the first review question.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What does large-file throughput require from the upload path?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For receipt images, the original file is the audit artifact, so an upload that silently becomes a thumbnail is a data-loss event even if the UI looks healthy. Measure the whole path: bytes accepted, upload duration, completed objects, incomplete multipart uploads, processing latency, and the age of the oldest pending receipt. The SLO should describe the user-visible obligation, such as the fraction of accepted receipts whose original is durable before processing begins, rather than only the HTTP response time. A 429 from a storage API is a capacity signal, not a reason to drop the receipt.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Capacity planning starts with bytes, not request count. If the service accepts &lt;code&gt;R&lt;/code&gt; receipts per minute and the p95 source size is &lt;code&gt;B&lt;/code&gt; bytes, the ingress estimate is &lt;code&gt;R * B&lt;/code&gt;; add headroom for retries, reprocessing, and a burst window. A worker pool sized for ten small images can be badly undersized for two large originals. Record size distributions, not just averages, because a few large files dominate bandwidth and temporary disk.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Multipart upload is the right shape when a large object must be transferred in parts and retried without restarting the entire file. The upload identifier belongs in durable job state. On success, mark the object complete and persist its key; on an abandoned attempt, abort the multipart upload and track that cleanup separately. A lifecycle rule for completed objects does not, by itself, make an incomplete upload part of the completed-object retention story. The runbook has to cover the half-finished state because retries, worker restarts, and deployments all create it; a dashboard that counts only completed objects will call this path healthy while storage continues to accumulate unfinished work.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The application should not hold a large file in Node memory while it waits for the storage request. Stream from the accepted input to the storage client or issue a bounded presigned upload, then verify the completed object before enqueueing receipt processing. The exact stream implementation depends on the storage client, so I would test it under the p99 file size and a deliberately interrupted connection before choosing worker limits.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  How can a deletion worker preserve an audit trail?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The worker below uses a generic HTTP contract rather than a vendor SDK. The important behavior is independent of the endpoint: select a bounded set of records, save the selection, delete only their recorded keys, retry transient throttling, and make the result observable. Secrets should come from a managed secret mechanism or an injected environment value; they should not be committed or printed in logs.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight go"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;package&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="s"&gt;"context"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="s"&gt;"fmt"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="s"&gt;"io"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="s"&gt;"net/http"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="s"&gt;"os"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="s"&gt;"time"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Deleter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;struct&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;BaseURL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;Token&lt;/span&gt;   &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;Client&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;http&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Client&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;func&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Deleter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Delete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;context&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Context&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;bucket&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;endpoint&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;BaseURL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;"/objects/"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;bucket&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;"/"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;++&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;req&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;http&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;NewRequestWithContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;http&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;MethodDelete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;endpoint&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;nil&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;nil&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;req&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Header&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"Authorization"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;"Bearer "&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Token&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Do&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;req&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;nil&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;_&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;readErr&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;io&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Copy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;io&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Discard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Close&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;readErr&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;nil&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;readErr&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;StatusCode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;http&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;StatusTooManyRequests&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="n"&gt;timer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;NewTimer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Duration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Second&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="k"&gt;select&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="k"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="n"&gt;timer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Stop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="k"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;timer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;C&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="k"&gt;continue&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;StatusCode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;http&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;StatusOK&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;StatusCode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;http&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;StatusMultipleChoices&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fmt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Errorf&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"delete %q: status %d"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;StatusCode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;nil&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fmt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Errorf&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"delete %q: retry budget exhausted"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;func&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;deleter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Deleter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;BaseURL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Getenv&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"OBJECT_STORE_URL"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;Token&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;   &lt;span class="n"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Getenv&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"OBJECT_STORE_TOKEN"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;Client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;http&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Timeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;30&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Second&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;deleter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Delete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;context&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Getenv&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"OBJECT_BUCKET"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Getenv&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"OBJECT_KEY"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;nil&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;fmt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Fprintln&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Stderr&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Exit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The sample intentionally does not list a prefix. A cleanup job that lists &lt;code&gt;users/alice/&lt;/code&gt; and deletes whatever looks old can remove a newly reprocessed receipt, miss a key moved by a migration, or cross an authorization boundary if the prefix is assembled incorrectly. Store the selection set before execution, include an idempotency key for the run, and make a retry safe to repeat. Depending on the storage contract, a successful delete may be idempotent; verify that behavior in the target service rather than assuming it. If the first attempt gets a 429, the job should retain its selection and retry that same decision; it should not run a new broad query and hope the result still means the same thing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Keep the token out of request URLs and logs. The OWASP guidance on secrets management is a useful baseline for storage, rotation, access control, and exposure review. A deletion log needs the record ID, object key, actor or job ID, decision, attempt count, and outcome, but it does not need the secret or the receipt contents.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Verify bytes first, then enable retention
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Start with a fixture set containing a small file, a p95-sized file, an interrupted multipart upload, an already-expired derivative, and two users whose identifiers share a prefix. Run the worker in dry-run mode, inspect the persisted selection, then execute against only that fixture set. Verify the original bytes and content type before processing, verify that the intended keys are absent after deletion, and check that unrelated keys remain. This is where a receipt archive earns its SLO: the test must prove that the original survives a worker restart, a retry, and a delayed lifecycle sweep, not merely that one happy-path request returns 2xx.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Alert on age, not just volume: oldest pending deletion, selected-versus-successful count, retry count, incomplete-upload count, and the percentage of accepted receipts without a durable original are more informative than one &lt;code&gt;cleanup_success&lt;/code&gt; counter. A zero-delete run may be correct for an empty queue. A growing oldest age is not.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rollback is a policy decision because deleting the only copy cannot be undone by the worker. Before physical deletion, a product may hide the image and hold the record during a grace period. That is unsuitable when a legal deletion deadline requires immediate removal. In that case, require a reviewed selection query, a small initial batch, and an independent audit record before widening the job.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The trade-offs that matter in production
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Choice&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Strength&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Cost or boundary&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Application-owned keys and metadata&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Clear ownership, retention intent, and auditability&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Requires a durable database record and migration discipline&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Explicit deletion worker&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Can be measured against a user-facing SLO&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Adds queueing, retries, authorization checks, and on-call signals&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Age-based lifecycle policy&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Simple housekeeping for temporary data&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Cannot express every business rule or necessarily meet a short deletion deadline&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Multipart upload&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Better retry behavior for large originals&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Requires upload-state tracking and abandoned-upload cleanup&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Self-hosted object storage&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Greater control over placement and operations&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Your team owns disks, upgrades, capacity, replication, and incidents&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Managed object storage&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Less storage infrastructure to operate&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Provider-specific policy surfaces and lock-in need review&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The recommendation is therefore conditional: use user-scoped immutable keys, explicit metadata, multipart transfer for genuinely large originals, and lifecycle rules only for data whose age is the policy. It is not suitable when the service needs transactional rename semantics, an immediate globally verified deletion guarantee, or a replication and retention control that the selected storage system does not provide; choose a storage design that exposes those guarantees and test them at the expected file-size distribution.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your mileage may vary. I am not sure a single throughput target can be stated without the source-size distribution, network shape, and processing SLO, so those measurements should be collected before capacity limits are fixed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  References
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/mpuoverview.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/mpuoverview.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Secrets_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Secrets_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Retry only the failed jobs you have selected, and cap each job at three attempts before sending it to a terminal queue. The important detail is the order of operations: publish the retry first, then acknowledge the dead-letter message, and make the worker idempotent because a standard queue can deliver a message more than once.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Short answer:&lt;/strong&gt; a dead-letter queue is a holding area, not a retry policy. List or inspect the failed messages, filter by a stable job ID, redrive the selected messages to the main queue, increment an application-level retry count, and record every decision. For a reservation-expiry job, the worker should re-check the reservation state before changing anything; a retry that arrives after the reservation was released must be harmless.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What should a targeted retry guarantee?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The useful guarantee here is bounded redelivery, not exactly-once execution. Exactly once is a tempting label, but a worker can fail after making a database change and before acknowledging the message. The next delivery is then legitimate. Idempotency is the mechanism that turns that duplicate delivery into a safe no-op.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For this example, a job has a stable &lt;code&gt;jobId&lt;/code&gt;, a &lt;code&gt;retryCount&lt;/code&gt;, and a payload containing the reservation to expire. The fixed hold window is 15 minutes. That number is a business rule in the example, not a queue feature: the worker compares the current reservation state and deadline, then decides whether there is still work to do.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The retry decision is deliberately narrow:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select &lt;code&gt;reservation:42&lt;/code&gt; and any other IDs explicitly approved for redrive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Refuse a message whose retry count is already 3.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Publish a new main-queue message with the incremented count.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acknowledge the original only after the publish succeeds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That ordering is the small part that prevents a manual retry tool from turning a recoverable failure into a lost job.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  How do you redrive only selected jobs in Node.js?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;RabbitMQ is a good concrete implementation for this pattern because dead lettering is built around exchanges and queues, while the application retains control of the message body. The sample below consumes from a DLQ, selects by &lt;code&gt;jobId&lt;/code&gt;, and republishes to the main queue. It uses a separate terminal queue for messages that have exhausted their retry budget.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;amqp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Channel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ConsumeMessage&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;amqplib&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ReservationExpiry&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;jobId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;reservationId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;expiresAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
